+	     only route to ASM_OUTPUT_EXTERNAL -- so on a target whose assembler
+	     requires a callee to be declared ahead of the call, the call is emitted
+	     with nothing declaring the callee and the unit is rejected.  Every other
+	     call in a module consumer reaches a decl somebody wrote and the front
+	     end marked external, which is why this is the one that got away.  */
+	  DECL_EXTERNAL (fndecl) = true;
